When my smile is radiant like sunshine,
When my dreams are woven beautifully enough,
Only then does the world applaud for me;
Only you worry that I might get hurt.

The whole world is waiting for me to fly higher,
Yet you ache with tenderness for my small wings,
Providing a resting place along my journey.

When I must be like a perfect child,
Fulfilling everyone's expectations,
You seem to uniquely appreciate
The ways I make mistakes and act foolish.

My imperfect dreams, you accompany me in imagining them;
My imperfect courage, you call it braver;
My imperfect tears, you wipe away with a smile;
My imperfect songs, you can sing them all.
My imperfect private thoughts, you keep them all in your heart;
This imperfect me, you always cherish like a treasure;
The love you give me might not be perfect, but it is the most beautiful.

(Interlude)

The whole world rushes me to grow up,
Yet you can always hold me gently in the palm of your hand,
Shielding me from
Those unknown winds and waves.

When I strive to be a perfect child,
Fulfilling everyone's expectations,
You never mention your own wishes,
Afraid of adding weight to my shoulders.

